{"1425":["<h4 style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700\">MENSURATION FORMULAS</h4><p style=\"color:#d32f2f;font-size:1.11em;font-weight:700\">2D AREA &amp; PERIMETER · 3D SURFACE AREA &amp; VOLUME</p><p style=\"font-weight:700\">a</p><p style=\"color:#5b6874;font-size:0.91em\">TSA = total surface area · CSA/LSA = curved/lateral surface area · l = slant height</p><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#cbdecc;border-color:#2e7d32\"><p style=\"color:#2e7d32;font-size:1.17em;font-weight:700\">2D SHAPES — Area &amp; Perimeter</p></div><i data-k=\"0\"></i><i data-k=\"1\"></i><i data-k=\"2\"></i><i data-k=\"3\"></i><i data-k=\"4\"></i><i data-k=\"5\"></i><i data-k=\"6\"></i><i data-k=\"7\"></i><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#c4d9ef;border-color:#1565c0\"><p style=\"color:#1565c0;font-size:1.17em;font-weight:700\">3D SHAPES — Surface Area &amp; Volume</p></div><i data-k=\"8\"></i><i data-k=\"9\"></i><i data-k=\"10\"></i><i data-k=\"11\"></i><i data-k=\"12\"></i><i data-k=\"13\"></i><i data-k=\"14\"></i><i data-k=\"15\"></i>",[["img/refp/mensuration-0.webp",672,3301,0,672,198,371],["img/refp/mensuration-0.webp",672,3301,204,672,197,371],["img/refp/mensuration-0.webp",672,3301,407,672,207,371],["img/refp/mensuration-0.webp",672,3301,620,672,202,371],["img/refp/mensuration-0.webp",672,3301,828,672,203,371],["img/refp/mensuration-0.webp",672,3301,1037,672,197,371],["img/refp/mensuration-0.webp",672,3301,1240,672,197,371],["img/refp/mensuration-0.webp",672,3301,1443,672,197,371],["img/refp/mensuration-0.webp",672,3301,1646,672,203,371],["img/refp/mensuration-0.webp",672,3301,1855,672,207,371],["img/refp/mensuration-0.webp",672,3301,2068,672,197,371],["img/refp/mensuration-0.webp",672,3301,2271,672,207,371],["img/refp/mensuration-0.webp",672,3301,2484,672,198,371],["img/refp/mensuration-0.webp",672,3301,2688,672,197,371],["img/refp/mensuration-0.webp",672,3301,2891,672,207,371],["img/refp/mensuration-0.webp",672,3301,3104,672,197,371]]],"1420":["<h4 style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700\">APTITUDE: MENSURATION &amp; INTEREST</h4><p style=\"color:#d32f2f;font-size:1.19em;font-weight:700\">SOLIDS (FRUSTUM, CONE, SPHERE) · SIMPLE &amp; COMPOUND INTEREST · VERIFIED WORKED SUMS</p><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#fdf5f8;border-color:#d81b60\"><div class=\"rb dk nb\" style=\"background:#d81b60\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#d81b60;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:700;background:#d81b60;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Solids — volume &amp; surface area</p></div><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt rc\"><thead><tr><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Solid</th><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Volume</th><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Surface area / note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Frustum (cut cone)</td><td data-h=\"Volume\">V = ⅓πh(R² + Rr + r²)</td><td data-h=\"Surface area / note\">slant l = √[h² + (R − r)²]; CSA = π(R + r)l; TSA = π(R + r)l + πR² + πr²</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Cone</td><td data-h=\"Volume\">V = ⅓πr²h</td><td data-h=\"Surface area / note\">l = √(r² + h²); CSA = πrl; TSA = πr(l + r)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Cylinder</td><td data-h=\"Volume\">V = πr²h</td><td data-h=\"Surface area / note\">CSA = 2πrh; TSA = 2πr(r + h)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Sphere / hemisphere</td><td data-h=\"Volume\">V = ⁴⁄₃πr³ / ⅔πr³</td><td data-h=\"Surface area / note\">SA = 4πr² / CSA 2πr², TSA 3πr²</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Hollow cylinder (pipe)</td><td data-h=\"Volume\">V = πh(R² − r²)</td><td data-h=\"Surface area / note\">material volume only</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Cuboid / cube</td><td data-h=\"Volume\">V = lbh / a³</td><td data-h=\"Surface area / note\">TSA = 2(lb + bh + hl) / 6a²; diagonal √(l² + b² + h²) / a√3</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Melting &amp; recasting</td><td data-h=\"Volume\">volume stays the same</td><td data-h=\"Surface area / note\">number of small solids = big volume ÷ one small volume</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#f6f9f6;border-color:#2e7d32\"><div class=\"rb dk nb\" style=\"background:#2e7d32\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#2e7d32;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:700;background:#2e7d32;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Simple &amp; compound interest</p></div><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt rc\"><thead><tr><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Case</th><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Formula</th><th style=\"background:#1b2a4a\">Note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Simple interest</td><td data-h=\"Formula\">SI = PRT/100</td><td data-h=\"Note\">A = P + SI</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Compound interest (yearly)</td><td data-h=\"Formula\">A = P(1 + R/100)ⁿ</td><td data-h=\"Note\">CI = A − P</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Half-yearly</td><td data-h=\"Formula\">A = P(1 + R/200)²ⁿ</td><td data-h=\"Note\">rate ÷ 2, periods × 2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Quarterly</td><td data-h=\"Formula\">A = P(1 + R/400)⁴ⁿ</td><td data-h=\"Note\">rate ÷ 4, periods × 4</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Different rates each year</td><td data-h=\"Formula\">A = P(1 + R₁/100)(1 + R₂/100)…</td><td data-h=\"Note\" class=\"e\"></td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">CI − SI, 2 years</td><td data-h=\"Formula\">P(R/100)²</td><td data-h=\"Note\">3 years: P(R/100)²(3 + R/100)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Effective annual rate</td><td data-h=\"Formula\">(1 + R/200)² − 1 (half-yearly)</td><td data-h=\"Note\">10 % half-yearly → 10.25 % a year</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Depreciation / population fall</td><td data-h=\"Formula\">A = P(1 − R/100)ⁿ</td><td data-h=\"Note\">growth: (1 + R/100)ⁿ</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#1a3a8f;font-weight:700\">Trick: spot the power</td><td data-h=\"Formula\">A/P = (p/q)ⁿ</td><td data-h=\"Note\">65536/50625 = (16/15)⁴ — learn 2ⁿ, 3ⁿ, 15⁴ = 50625, 16⁴ = 65536</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class=\"rb\" style=\"background:#f4f8fc;border-color:#1565c0\"><div class=\"rb dk nb\" style=\"background:#1565c0\"><p style=\"color:#fff;background:#1565c0;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:700;background:#1565c0;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Worked sums (answers checked by code)</p></div><p style=\"font-weight:700\">1. TNPSC Q161: frustum, h = 30 cm, radii 28 cm and 7 cm. Volume?</p><p style=\"color:#37474f\">⅓ × 22/7 × 30 × (28² + 28×7 + 7²) = 10 × 22/7 × 1029 = 10 × 22 × 147<span style=\"color:#15202b\"> → </span><span style=\"color:#2e7d32\"><b>32340 cm³ → (A)</b></span></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\">2. Same frustum: slant height?</p><p style=\"color:#37474f\">l = √[30² + (28 − 7)²] = √(900 + 441) = √1341<span style=\"color:#15202b\"> → </span><span style=\"color:#2e7d32\"><b>≈ 36.62 cm</b></span></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\">3. TNPSC Q156: ₹50,625 → ₹65,536 at 13⅓ % p.a., compounded half-yearly. Time? half-year rate = (40/3)/2 % = 1/15; 65536/50625 = (16/15)⁴ → 4 half-years<span style=\"color:#15202b\"> → </span><span style=\"color:#2e7d32\"><b>2 years → (B)</b></span></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\">4. ₹10,000 at 10 % for 2 years. CI − SI?</p><p style=\"color:#37474f\">P(R/100)² = 10000 × 0.01<span style=\"color:#15202b\"> → </span><span style=\"color:#2e7d32\"><b>₹100</b></span></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\">5. ₹10,000 at 10 % for 3 years. CI − SI?</p><p style=\"color:#37474f\">P(R/100)²(3 + R/100) = 100 × 3.1<span style=\"color:#15202b\"> → </span><span style=\"color:#2e7d32\"><b>₹310</b></span></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\">6. 10 % p.a. compounded half-yearly. Effective annual rate?</p><p style=\"color:#37474f\">(1.05)² − 1 = 0.1025<span style=\"color:#15202b\"> → </span><span style=\"color:#2e7d32\"><b>10.25 %</b></span></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\">7. Machine ₹20,000 depreciates 10 % a year. Value after 2 years?</p><p style=\"color:#37474f\">20000 × 0.9²<span style=\"color:#15202b\"> → </span><span style=\"color:#2e7d32\"><b>₹16,200</b></span></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\">8. Metal sphere r = 6 cm melted into balls r = 2 cm. How many?</p><p style=\"color:#37474f\">(6/2)³<span style=\"color:#15202b\"> → </span><span style=\"color:#2e7d32\"><b>27</b></span></p><p style=\"font-weight:700\">9. Cone r = 7 cm, h = 24 cm. Volume?</p><p style=\"color:#37474f\">⅓ × 22/7 × 49 × 24<span style=\"color:#15202b\"> → </span><span style=\"color:#2e7d32\"><b>1232 cm³</b></span></p></div>",[]]}